abe90e69f5267b3ea (all four tests passed) reproduced the two earlier witnesses and showed that the node which took over from a follower whose Promise carried the StopSign ended inflated in its own accepted index: accepted 7 over six indices of content, read(5) None and a one-element decided log (event 13), with both other nodes also at accepted 7 and a one-element read (events 12, 14), so the corruption propagates across the authority change. A behavior was added for the candidate leader syncing from a follower, the applicability fact now lists that third producer instance, the interpretation covers all four receipts with their controls, and the last open half of the registered gap is targeted by a successor experiment that enables snapshots through a snapshot-capable entry type.\\\"),\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[interp],\\\"knowledge\\\":[fact,kr],\n \\\"investigations\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":QC,\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Whether a snapshot-capable configuration (Snapshot::use_snapshots() true) reproduces the same inflation in the two-follower reconnection scenario, as the branch analysis predicts, or takes the snapshot branch and avoids it.\\\"}],\n \\\"experiment\\\":exp}\njson.dump(up, open('update.json','w'), indent=1); print('update written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_09-22-17-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -c 1200\"","aggregated_output":"update written\n{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"d99e3b9fb63f4d89b4e0c59b4352dd5b\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 1334.7299144660064, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_re